974609375, 0.028656005859375, -0.01331329345703125, -0.01145172119140625, -0.002292633056640625, 0.0236968994140625, 0.005794525146484375, -0.01140594482421875, 0.02972412109375, -0.038360595703125, 0.0172576904296875, 0.006610870361328125, -0.0053863525390625, 0.01800537109375, -0.00235748291015625, 0.039703369140625, -0.00095367431640625, 0.053985595703125, 0.0018014907836914062, 0.040802001953125, -0.007526397705078125, -0.001220703125, -0.00047969818115234375, -0.0160064697265625, 0.0083465576171875, 0.000514984130859375, -0.0205230712890625, 0.0251007080078125, 0.0537109375, -0.019805908203125, -0.0208587646484375, -0.0278778076171875, 0.024505615234375, -0.0181732177734375, 0.00494384765625, 0.047821044921875, 0.031341552734375, -0.0016355514526367188, -0.03558349609375, -0.0119781494140625, -0.01181793212890625, 0.00933837890625, -0.026824951171875, 0.01715087890625, -0.0189056396484375, -0.024261474609375, -0.0138397216796875, -0.01035308837890625, 0.030731201171875, 0.0105438232421875, -0.01270294189453125, -0.007724761962890625], "payload": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "text": "Large-scale image generation has advanced through improvements in data scale, quality, rebalancing, and recaptioning. However, conventional pipelines typically optimize task-specific datasets in isolation. A key challenge lies not only in curating each task-specific corpus, but also in organizing heterogeneous supervision according to the dependencies among generative capabilities. We introduce a \\textbf{capability-driven data infrastructure} that integrates capability-specific supervision construction with capability-aligned curriculum scheduling. This infrastructure comprises three specialized yet interoperable data engines that generate complementary relational supervision for text-image grounding, inter-image transformation, and image-knowledge association. Caption experts further align text-to-image (T2I) and editing supervision across tasks and levels of granularity. A multi-stage curriculum jointly evolves task composition, visual concept distribution, data quality, and image resolution in accordance with the dependency order of capability acquisition. Capability-aware evaluation closes the loop through targeted retrieval, expert construction, and gap-aware resampling. At scale, this framework curates a 440M-image T2I corpus, 120M editing pairs, and over 27M image-entity pairs. Using this infrastructure, we train multimodal diffusion models from scratch at two scales, with 3B and 6B parameters, respectively. We conduct quantitative evaluation on CPI-Bench, as well as qualitative assessments across diverse text-to-image and editing scenarios. Experimental results demonstrate broad visual coverage, versatile rendering, and effective transfer across generative capabilities."}}